WEBVTT

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:21.910
Katana Samurai  Rindo

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.670
Chitose Aoba

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:27.040
<b>S'Alright!</b>

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:27.040
December 28th 06:52 Fukuoka

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:27.040
<b>Welcome to Fukuoka, Kyushu</b>

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:09.730
Whew, I thought we were goners.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.850
I told you...

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:20.220
that crossing the Kanmon Strait in 
a little boat like that was reckless.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:37.880
Me and my dad, and my dad's dad, 
we were all born on stormy seas...

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.820
In the month since we've left Michinoku,

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:36.760
your foolhardy personality has almost 
gotten us killed so many times.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:38.900
Who cares?

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:42.000
We made it to Kyushu alive.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.530
So it's all good!

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:50.640
Are you hungry?

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:55.080
You must be hungry.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.400
W-Well... yeah...

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.760
Sera Kurashiki

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.160
Then leave it to Sera!

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:10.490
My mom always told me to be nice 
to people who are in trouble.

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:12.170
Here it is!

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.670
A Card Device!

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:16.710
Activate!

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:25.930
Ultimate Dinosaur  Orichalcum Tyranno

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:30.680
I'll introduce you.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:33.320
That's Orichalcum Tyranno!

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:37.830
I'm his mother!

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:43.700
Hey, it's Tyranno!

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:46.460
Wait, Tyranno!

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:48.450
You guys, don't get too close! It's dangerous!

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:49.850
He's so big!

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:51.090
He's awesome!

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:52.960
Hey, let me ride him, too!

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:56.210
I'm sorry. Next time, okay?

00:03:56.810 --> 00:03:58.150
Next time?

00:03:58.150 --> 00:03:59.710
You'd better promise!

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:02.470
Yup! I double super-duper promise!

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:04.510
Okay, it's a promise!

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:07.830
Bye!

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:08.710
See you next time! Bye-bye!

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:09.500
What's going on?

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:12.580
They're not afraid of the Z/X at all.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:14.180
They came right up to it!

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:15.730
Look.

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:20.240
C'mon, give me a discount.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:23.240
Humans and Z/X are living together?

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:26.450
It's hard to believe,

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:30.630
but that's what life is like in this town.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:35.830
Alexander rules this town.

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:37.130
Alexander?

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:40.380
One of the Nine Worthies?

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:44.630
I don't really know, but something like that.

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:48.370
Alexander's really violent.

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:51.500
When he gets out of control, it's really bad...

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.470
But normally, he's nice to both humans and Z/X.

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:56.790
He's not a bad king.

00:04:57.150 --> 00:05:02.660
It's true that everyone here, 
Z/X and human alike, is smiling.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:05.650
I've never seen a place like this.

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:10.160
That's probably thanks 
to Mikado, not Alexander.

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:12.660
Who's Mikado?

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:18.420
Hmm... I think he said he 
was Alexander's strategist.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:19.660
A strategist?

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:23.800
Someone who provides his lord with 
advice on strategy and tactics?

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:25.000
Yeah, that.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:26.970
He gives him advice all the time.

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:29.870
Alexander doesn't usually listen, though.

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:33.560
<b>Hata Garrison</b>

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.560
We're here!

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:35.410
Wait, what?!

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:37.690
This is a Defense Force garrison!

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:40.810
December 28th 07:22 Hata Garrison

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:39.050
That's right.

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:40.810
I live here now.

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:42.820
We really shouldn't be here!

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:44.660
Huh? Why?

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:47.570
I've... got my reasons.

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:50.320
I don't understand complicated stuff!

00:05:57.770 --> 00:05:59.080
It'll be fine.

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:03.580
You were part of the Michinoku force.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:06.550
Now that the territory is divided,

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:10.340
they can't easily contact a distant base.

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:13.060
That's true, but...

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:15.840
Let's eat our meal, then.

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:17.850
Let's eat.

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:19.350
Okay, go ahead!

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:23.360
This taste brings back memories!

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:26.260
It's not bad.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:33.240
Anyway, this place sure is bustling.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:35.700
Everyone's in high spirits.

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:38.450
'Cause the invasion's about to start.

00:06:38.450 --> 00:06:39.250
Invasion?

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:44.010
These people aren't going 
to team up with the Z/X

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:45.750
to attack some other town, are they?

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:49.260
Isn't a Defense Force only supposed 
to be used for defense?

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:53.510
I told you, I don't understand complicated stuff.

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:56.930
I thought this place was peaceful,

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:58.510
but you're going to invade somewhere?

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:07.030
Mikado, good morning!

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:21.170
Mikado Kurosaki

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:21.170
Are you the Z/X user that Sera brought in?

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:26.420
Come with me.

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:30.420
<b>Heart</b>

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:32.550
What's your name?

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:34.430
Yes! Sera Kurashiki!

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:37.990
Sera, I don't need you here.

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:39.890
Go back to your room.

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:41.420
Aww...

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:44.840
Chitose Aoba.

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:46.190
Rindo.

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:48.980
I'm Mikado Kurosaki.

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:54.820
I serve as strategist to Alexander, 
legendary hero and ruler of Fukuoka.

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:59.880
And you've cajoled the 
Z/X and the Defense Force

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:02.430
into starting a war, huh?

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:04.830
Getting little kids like Sera involved, too?

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:07.150
Did you see the town?

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:09.840
What did you think?

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:13.840
It was nice.

00:08:16.630 --> 00:08:21.020
This city is a utopia that 
Alexander and I built together,

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:26.610
when I commanded the Defense 
Force and he led the Z/X.

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:29.080
You created it?

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:29.860
Yes.

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:33.860
And it was by no means easy.

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:38.620
There were endless battles,

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:41.370
and endless blood was shed.

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:46.360
But even if we did win this 
utopia for ourselves,

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:54.140
is it really right for those of us with power 
to simply stay here and enjoy the peace?

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:57.510
Isn't that mere laziness?

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:01.510
Outside the city,

00:09:01.510 --> 00:09:03.530
there are people whose 
livelihoods are threatened,

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:06.550
who don't have enough food to live.

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:11.530
Can you tell me that ignoring 
them is the right thing to do?

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:15.130
But that doesn't mean it's 
okay to resort to violence.

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:18.410
It's true that if we invade another area,

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:20.530
there may be war.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:23.910
People will die on both sides if that happens.

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:26.290
And it will cause chaos among the civilians.

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:32.310
But after that will come eternal peace.

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:35.170
I have that power!

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:38.950
Alexander and I,

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:41.140
along with the strong warriors gathered here,

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:43.230
will expand our territory.

00:09:44.420 --> 00:09:46.960
We will reunite Japan,

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:49.230
and bring an end to the 
chaos that has reigned

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:52.360
since the appearance 
of the Black Points.

00:09:58.890 --> 00:10:00.310
Chitose Aoba.

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:06.200
If you agree with my ambitions, 
I would welcome you.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:10.250
I won't force you.

00:10:10.780 --> 00:10:14.790
If you want to leave, 
you may do as you wish.

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:23.310
As always, you have a way 
with words, my strategist.

00:10:24.280 --> 00:10:27.460
We don't need the help of that wanderer.

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:32.770
I can conquer a country or two by myself.

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:32.770
Nine Worthies  Alexander

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:37.330
You can never have too many forces.

00:10:37.330 --> 00:10:42.460
And wanderers can be surprisingly useful.

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:47.790
December 28th 16:07 Hata Garrison Barracks

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:50.110
What do you think, Rindo?

00:10:50.110 --> 00:10:55.110
What that Mikado guy says isn't wrong.

00:10:56.120 --> 00:10:57.110
But...

00:10:57.110 --> 00:10:58.280
But?

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:01.950
It seems dangerous to trust him.

00:11:03.670 --> 00:11:05.810
I think so too, but...

00:11:06.440 --> 00:11:09.580
He's trying to do something.

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:13.560
That's way better than doing nothing.

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:13.560
November 19th 03:08 Miyagino Garrison

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:16.590
<b>Danger
Authorization Required</b>

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:19.950
<i>Bingo!</i>

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:25.330
Little late to figure it out now!

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:27.580
I swear...

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:32.580
"Our conventional weapons 
cannot fight the Z/X," they said?

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:36.590
And every other word 
out of their mouths was,

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:40.090
"We need to conserve our forces 
for when they're really needed."

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:44.090
If they aren't needed now, when 
will we need them, you morons?

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:47.400
I'll do it alone if I have to.

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:50.950
These people need help, 
and I can't ignore them any longer!

00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:56.380
But that was just arrogance.

00:11:56.380 --> 00:12:00.880
Even with a Card Device, 
there was nothing I could do alone.

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:02.360
Bestial Laundryman  Were-Raccoon

00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:04.940
I remember.

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:09.370
I remember the tears you 
shed for one of us, a Z/X,

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:11.560
Dawn Mantis  Glory Scythe

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:11.870
beings that threaten humanity.

00:12:17.480 --> 00:12:19.380
I want to help people.

00:12:20.150 --> 00:12:24.790
Anyone who's weak, 
whether they're human or Z/X.

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:27.230
I know that.

00:12:27.230 --> 00:12:31.140
That's why I let you capture me.

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:43.400
I was prepared to die once.

00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:49.040
I would gladly sacrifice anything for you.

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:54.760
You are my lord.

00:12:54.760 --> 00:12:58.840
No matter what decision 
you make, I will obey it.

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:01.420
Thank you, Rindo.

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:09.010
Sera, what happened?

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:10.980
"What happened"? The enemy's attacking!

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:12.020
The enemy?

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:20.070
December 28th 16:49 Sea Near Fukuoka

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:22.570
Lightning Tourmaline   Tourmaline Hawk

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:28.570
The Tourmaline Hawk. 
A bird-shaped Gigantic.

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:29.950
Gigantic?

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:36.240
A general term of the Red 
World for giant creatures

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:37.960
created to fight Bravers.

00:13:38.740 --> 00:13:43.960
They were made with an instinct to 
become violent when they sense a Braver.

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:46.470
Then now...

00:13:46.920 --> 00:13:51.780
They sense the greatest of the Bravers, 
Alexander of the Nine Worthies,

00:13:51.780 --> 00:13:52.970
and it has roused them.

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:57.980
You've got the air force 
under your control, too?

00:13:58.430 --> 00:14:02.990
I told you. I control the 
Defense Force of Kyushu.

00:14:05.450 --> 00:14:07.730
Target: the Tourmaline Hawks.

00:14:07.730 --> 00:14:09.240
Number of enemies: 23.

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:10.860
Attack!

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:30.470
We got them!

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:32.810
Don't waste too much effort on them.

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:33.470
Roger!

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:48.950
Full-speed retreat!

00:14:49.420 --> 00:14:52.120
With our current equipment, 
we don't stand a chance!

00:14:56.150 --> 00:14:58.220
Thank you, Rindo.

00:14:58.220 --> 00:15:00.080
Think nothing of it.

00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:01.960
They're going to attack the town!

00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:06.170
No, they're only after Alexander.

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:09.590
With that bait dangling right in 
front of them, they'll ignore the town.

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:11.880
Then get him out here!

00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:13.350
He's been here the whole time.

00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:15.850
Weren't you listening?

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:18.490
I just told you.

00:15:18.490 --> 00:15:22.410
They become more violent 
when they sense a Braver.

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:32.990
Alexander, time to show them the 
unwavering power of a king!

00:15:39.690 --> 00:15:42.620
Alexander, are you listening?

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:44.140
Alexander!

00:15:44.900 --> 00:15:46.500
My strategist...

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:50.100
I've found prey worthy of me.

00:15:50.100 --> 00:15:51.010
What?

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:55.760
Something's coming!

00:16:13.050 --> 00:16:17.990
Splendid! The raptor tyrant, 
beautiful and proud!

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:20.490
Come to me!

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:22.000
Violent Hawk's Eye  Hawk's Eye

00:16:22.280 --> 00:16:22.870
Is that...

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:23.750
It can't be...

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:25.790
A Hawk's Eye?

00:16:26.980 --> 00:16:28.250
Come to me.

00:16:31.370 --> 00:16:34.220
I will reward you personally!

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:45.020
He took out that huge Z/X with one hit?

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:48.520
I see.

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:50.530
That reward was not enough, then?

00:16:56.050 --> 00:16:58.280
You amuse me.

00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:03.030
Very well. I shall grant any reward you desire!

00:17:03.490 --> 00:17:04.540
Bucephalus!

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:07.420
Black Horse of Conquest  Bucephalus

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:07.420
Mikado!

00:17:07.850 --> 00:17:11.290
Behold my battle!

00:17:12.660 --> 00:17:14.170
This is Gryphon 1!

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:16.170
Now entering the mission area!

00:17:16.850 --> 00:17:17.930
Roger.

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:43.270
Wow...

00:17:43.270 --> 00:17:45.910
Is that the power of the Nine Worthies?

00:17:50.760 --> 00:17:53.300
What a powerful glow...

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:56.820
Then I shall vent my sorrows on you!

00:18:05.320 --> 00:18:09.850
All ground forces! Your first 
priority is to evacuate all civilians.

00:18:09.850 --> 00:18:10.560
HQ, roger!

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:13.620
Alexander! The town is taking damage.

00:18:13.620 --> 00:18:14.820
Control yourself.

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:15.840
Laughable!

00:18:16.230 --> 00:18:20.320
A few casualties are meaningless in the 
face of the holiness that is my battle!

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:22.500
Are you scared, Mikado?

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:24.830
Hey, is he crazy?!

00:18:25.850 --> 00:18:26.690
Sera!

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:28.330
Leave it to me!

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:35.920
Go, Tyranno!

00:18:42.210 --> 00:18:44.070
Hurry! This way!

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:48.310
I am the one, the absolute!

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:03.700
Ruler's Earthquake Spear!

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:08.960
You will return to dust!

00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:23.770
That was entertaining.

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:26.470
December 29th 01:15 Hata Garrison

00:19:27.240 --> 00:19:30.710
December 29th 01:17 Hata Garrison - Mikado's Room

00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:33.480
Just wait a little longer, Kasuga.

00:19:33.970 --> 00:19:36.980
I'll bring you back to life.

00:19:38.040 --> 00:19:39.080
I will.

00:19:41.870 --> 00:19:42.990
What do you want?

00:19:44.300 --> 00:19:47.580
What did you think of my battle today,

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:49.450
my strategist?

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:52.620
Brilliant... is what I'd like to say, but...

00:19:53.720 --> 00:19:54.880
You're unsatisfied?

00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:56.790
Of course.

00:19:56.790 --> 00:19:59.310
Do you know how much damage you caused?

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:02.550
If you call yourself a king,

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:05.160
you need to show more 
consideration for your people.

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:08.890
Otherwise, you might start a rebellion.

00:20:09.200 --> 00:20:12.390
Stopping that rebellion is your job, right?

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:15.320
I am uninterested in rule.

00:20:15.320 --> 00:20:18.400
The only goal in my life is conquest.

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:25.660
To make every city, country, 
and land in this world mine.

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:29.250
I'll leave everything else to you.

00:20:30.340 --> 00:20:31.660
Very well.

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:35.370
Then I'll take the supplies we 
were saving for the invasion

00:20:35.370 --> 00:20:37.680
and give them to the victims of today's battle.

00:20:37.680 --> 00:20:38.800
No complaints, I assume?

00:20:40.310 --> 00:20:41.790
Do as you please.

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:49.060
You're not so incompetent as to 
let something so insignificant

00:20:49.550 --> 00:20:53.560
interfere with the invasion, right?

00:20:54.310 --> 00:20:55.390
Of course not.

00:20:55.820 --> 00:20:59.470
I'm counting on you, my strategist.

00:21:08.890 --> 00:21:11.700
